description: Standards for writing NestJS service files
globs: src/**/*.service.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

## NestJS Service Standards

### TypeORM
- NEVER manually check `deletedAt` — TypeORM soft deletes filter it automatically
- Always use repository pattern via `@InjectRepository`
- Raw queries must include `AND deleted_at IS NULL` if soft deletes apply

### No N+1 queries
- NEVER call the database inside a loop
- Fetch all records in one query using `WHERE id IN (...)`, then iterate in memory with a Map:
  ```ts
  const ids = items.map(i => i.userId)
  const users = await this.userRepo.findBy({ id: In(ids) })
  const map = new Map(users.map(u => [u.id, u]))
  ```

### Return values
- NEVER return `null` — throw `NotFoundException` or return `[]` / `{}`
- Every method must have an explicit return type — no implicit `any`

### Enums
- NEVER use string enums or raw strings for status/type comparisons
- Always use integer-valued TypeScript enums

### Constants
- NEVER hardcode magic values — put them in `src/common/constants/`

### Inputs
- Accept DTOs as parameters — never accept raw `any` or untyped objects
- All normalization (trim, lowercase) must happen in the DTO, not here

### Entity defaults
- NEVER set `isActive: true` or similar defaults in service code — defaults belong on the entity

### Errors
- Throw NestJS built-in exceptions: `NotFoundException`, `BadRequestException`, `ForbiddenException`
- Never silently return null when a record is expected but not found
